#!/usr/bin/env vml
# ============================================================================
#   Bob: builds Visualised projects. Pick a project (any folder in the repo
#   with a recipe: Visualised itself, Mountie, Bob...) and Bob shows a card
#   for each of its builds: where it's built (this computer, or another one
#   over SSH), a light, the stage it's at and the time it's taken, and every
#   line of it on its own tab. Build one, or Build all at once.
#
#   The recipes: each project's recipe.vml, in VML (what to build and where;
#   see tools/bob/recipe.py). The machines: ~/.config/bob/machines.vml
#   (Project ▾ > Machines…). New project makes a recipe for you.
#   Set up… says where the repo is (~/projects/vml-github unless you say);
#   BOB_REPO in the environment wins.
#   GitHub: Bob keeps an eye on the repo's Actions too (with the gh command,
#   signed in): a run starting or finishing brings him to the front with a
#   notification, and the GitHub tab shows every run and the steps of the
#   one going now.
#   Away from desk locks this computer and the Windows machines, and logs how
#   long you were away (~/.local/share/bob/away.csv).
#   Run it as a program: chmod +x Bob.vml, then ./Bob.vml
#
#   Made with Visualised.
# ============================================================================

@Window Bob
Title=Bob build tool
Version=2.9
AppBar=true
Terms=https://tiny-web.uk/terms.php
About=Bob builds your Visualised projects, here and on any machine you can reach over SSH. https://bob.vml.onl
Icon=bob.png
TitleBar=Own
BorderBrush=#1F2937
BorderThickness=2
Width=780
Height=640
MinWidth=780
MinHeight=520
OnOpened=Opened

@Canvas c
Parent=Bob
Background=#F3F4F6

